WEBVTT

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.140
What's this?

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.390
Who knows...

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.280
An old man?

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.990
No!

00:01:51.130 --> 00:02:00.970
As the Pureleine, you'll use the Pureleine Computer, find the Bad Items, and extract the Bad Cards from them.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.980
Doremi-chan, Hadzuki-chan, Aiko-chan.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:11.440
From now on, as the Pureleine, please collect the Bad Cards.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.070
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
The Arrival of Oyajiide!?

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:28.960
That was great, everyone, becoming the Pureleine.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.170
What Pureleine? You're all just Ojamajos.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.470
Doremi, do you know how to use a computer?

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.180
Oh, it's easy.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.020
Let's see, let's see...

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.240
What the?

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.190
Nothing's happening.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.480
Don't just touch it like that.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.190
Is it broken?

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.030
No way.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.790
It turned on.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.750
It must be set so that only the Pureleine can use it.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.830
I really want to become a Pureleine too!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.050
Huh? What's that?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.340
It looks like a Witch Frog.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.830
Is it Plush-chan's relative?

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.950
My relatives aren't that ugly.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:25.810
So loud...

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.630
It talked!

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.390
It did.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.150
Ah, I can't sleep like this.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.690
What a nice body...

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.900
What are you, you old man?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:45.370
I am Alexander Oyajiide, a wizard!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.330
Ya really are an old man.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.380
Listen up.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:53.090
I am living in this computer right now, acting as a judge for the Bad Items.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:58.050
I am here to tell the Pureleine whether the items they bring to me are Bad Items or not.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.550
Judge?

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:03.030
That's because I have a special power.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:09.060
All I need is one look and I can tell whether an item has a Bad Card inside it.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.360
Anyway, where are the Pureleine?

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:14.600
Don't tell me...!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.440
We are the Pureleine!

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.960
You're kidding, right?

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.440
Are you three really witches?

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.610
Yes.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.120
We are witch apprentices that just passed the level 6 exam.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.080
Level 6 witch apprentices!?

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.370
And they're also Ojamajos.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.030
Level 6...

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.010
And Ojamajos...

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:39.340
No! If I have to rely on these little kids, I'll never be able to get out of here!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.010
What do you mean?

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:49.370
I have to stay in here until after I collect all of the Bad Cards that were left in this world.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:50.180
Who's that?

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.220
That's me.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.600
Really?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:57.780
I used to be the most handsome fortune telling wizard in the Witch World!

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.980
Furthermore, I was a phantom thief!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:07.990
But since I was bored of my job, I snuck into the Witch World to steal some treasure.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.930
While there, I chanced upon some of the Bad Cards.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.960
They're actually quite popular among collectors...

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:26.110
But before I collected my payment, I had lost the cards.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:31.690
They then discovered that I stole the cards and changed me into this form.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:35.230
Then they sealed me into this computer!

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.730
I see.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:40.710
You were the most famous fortune teller wizard, as well as with a phantom thief,

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:43.400
but you were found out the first time you stole something, weren't you?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.770
And you were found guilty of losing the Bad Cards.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:50.200
Wow this guy's a mess.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.500
No, I can understand how he feels.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:56.360
I want the old days to come back already.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.000
But I have to take care of these Ojamajos.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.230
Don't tell me that you were found out by these girls and turned into that form?

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:08.590
I want them to gain power quickly and become fabulous witches!

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.670
Oh, how it seems like you've gone through such pain too.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.350
It's like a match made in heaven.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.710
That's enough talk. Hurry up and find those Bad Items!

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:21.680
That's right.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.780
The Bad Cards are very rare, so we may get a bundle if you find them.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.910
Maybe I'll even get a bonus from the Queen...!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:34.330
You weren't able to become a Pureleine because of those selfish thoughts.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:39.610
If we don't find the Bad Cards, then I'm stuck here!

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.060
That's your own problem!

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:41.700
What!?

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.470
Their friendship was broken so quickly.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:48.580
But Oyaji-san is right.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.600
We must find the Bad Items quickly.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.610
Yes, just like the one at Kanae-chan's family steakhouse.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:57.210
There may be Bad Cards elsewhere.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.780
Okay, let's go!

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.350
Yeah!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.860
But just how do you plan to find them?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.560
Oh yeah.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.970
How about we ask people to bring their items to us?

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:10.830
That could work.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.700
We'll put flyers in the store and pass them out too.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.870
Hey, who'll look after the store?

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:23.330
If you bring over your items, we'll check them for free!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.720
Please bring them over to the Maho-dou.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.050
We can even check large items.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:31.260
Thank you very much.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.270
What are you girls doing?

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.820
It's so hot!

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:38.390
And I'm not not not getting it at all!

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:42.600
Hey, do you guys have any suspicious items in your homes?

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.640
No, why would we?

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:51.240
But since you brought it up, our newly installed air conditioner has been acting a bit strange.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.320
Really?

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:56.520
Everyone thinks my new jokes aren't funny.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.450
Just like an air conditioner, so cold!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.660
We've passed out so many flyers, so it should have done something at least.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.450
Yeah!

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.640
What IS this!?

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.680
What kind of advertisement were you guys doing!?

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.640
Those people want us to check all of THIS?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.140
Yeah.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:27.120
A lot of people also wanted their items checked up front.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:30.050
Did everyone think that this place is a garbage dump?

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:33.900
But there might be Bad Items in that pile.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.820
Let's check them out anyway.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.200
Wrong! That's not a Bad Item!

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.380
Not this one either, right?

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.630
What the heck!?

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.340
None of these are Bad Items.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.050
It's probably all just regular garbage.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:58.190
But some people wanted to have their items checked up front.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.850
You're right, let's go see them.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.800
Good afternoon, we're from the Maho-dou.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.650
After we bought this raccoon statue, our luck has turned bad.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.360
Sweet, this might be good.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.720
No, this raccoon isn't any good, really.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:18.960
Thank goodness.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:21.540
No, like I said, this isn't any good at all.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.040
Well, let's check it out anyway.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.500
This is just a normal raccoon.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.330
Hey, that computer just talked!

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.970
But what was the bad luck you were talking about?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:39.190
I lost 3 kilograms, but then I gained 5.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:47.020
If this goes on, I don't think I'll ever get out of here.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:52.700
I am the world's unluckiest wizard!

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:57.240
In the end, we couldn't find any...

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.870
I don't think this'll be easy...

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.580
It's hard being a Pureleine.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:06.230
Hey, we should check the items in our own homes.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:09.380
After all, I am the world's unluckiest pretty girl,

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.750
so it's possible we have a Bad Item here.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:12.790
Impossible, impossible.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.460
What's with that?

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:21.100
But checkin' these items one by one really limits us, y'know?

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:25.720
It'd be nice if Oyaji-san could give us a hint regarding where the Bad Items are.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.040
Well, let's jus' ask him.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.340
What is it? Checking something again?

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:36.280
I doubt you have anything good for me.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:41.450
'Kay, you can say that, but those Bad Items ain't gonna come lookin' fer us, which means yer stuck here.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.030
Do you know where Bad Items can normally be found?

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:46.870
Well I was a fortune teller...

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:50.430
Okay... Let me give this a shot.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.970
Do ya see anything?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.760
A Bad Item is...

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.970
over there!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:08.010
There is a tall building there.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.660
And there is a flowing river.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:13.650
A river?

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.520
And there are green trees.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.010
The scene on the television matches perfectly to what Oyaji is saying.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.280
Is that really where it is?

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.600
Ooohhh, yes, yes.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.040
I see the exact same place.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.660
Eh? Isn't that Hadzuki-chan's papa?

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:38.120
Director Fujiwara's newest work, slated to come out this fall, may not finish on time.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:43.720
The filming has fallen behind schedule and the main lead, Tsuehiro Koyuri, is injured.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:49.980
With the filming interrupted, people are saying that perhaps this film is cursed.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.070
That looks bad.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:55.350
It's just like what Oyaji said, so maybe a Bad Item's causing it?

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.320
Papa...

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.870
Okay, let's go over there right now.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:26.640
Your dad is filming somewhere near here, right?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.520
Yes.

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.170
Ah, ain't that it?

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.690
That's Sorimayu!

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.170
Doremi-chan.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:44.680
We're here to find the Bad Item.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.120
I-I knew that.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.150
Hadzuki.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:55.790
Why are you here?

00:12:56.490 --> 00:13:00.360
Um, everyone wanted to see the filming.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.900
Please.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.990
We won't trouble you.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:05.340
Can they, Papa?

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:09.360
Well, right now things aren't going so well.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.310
You girls might get bored.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.020
That's fine.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:13.920
I see...

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.480
Then sure, go ahead.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.860
Thank you!

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:22.940
Hey.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.950
It looks like filming hasn't started yet.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.620
Did something happen?

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:31.360
Yeah, the director has been waiting like this for a few days.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:34.840
He thinks that the background for this scene is lacking something.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:37.230
He's troubled by all this thinking.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.710
Just what exactly is missing?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.420
Well, the director is a perfectionist, so...

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:48.120
Is it because of Papa that the filming isn't proceeding?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.660
That's not true.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:51.930
This is definitely the work of a Bad Item!

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:52.880
That's right.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:55.690
If we can find the Bad Card, then the rest of the filming will go smoothly.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:56.810
Come on, let's start looking.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.340
But...

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:04.400
The most suspicious items are the ones that Hadzuki-chan's papa is using.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.890
Well let's just ask him then!

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.270
Um...

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:13.030
Can we borrow that chair fer a second?

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.560
And that megaphone and those sunglasses...

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:17.000
What on earth for?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:20.460
Um, Papa, I'm really sorry to disturb you at work.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:25.510
But could we borrow those things for a second?

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.690
Hadzuki, didn't I tell you not to bother me?

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:34.180
But there might be something wrong with the things you are using.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.670
Something wrong?

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:37.850
Are you saying that something bad will happen to me?

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.150
That's what we want to investigate.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:46.310
This chair, this megaphone, and these sunglasses are my treasured items from my first film.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.320
There shouldn't be anything wrong with them!

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:51.370
I'm sorry.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:55.740
Papa doesn't seem to be in a good mood. He's usually not like this.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.230
We can't do anything about that.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.430
Things look bad, that's why.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.640
Let's check some other things first.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:02.460
Yeah.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.850
Where is it?

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.430
The sun is settin' already.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.000
Goodness gracious.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.900
You girls aren't reliable at all.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.900
Is there REALLY a Bad Item here?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:26.780
What!?

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.990
You Ojamajos dare question me?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.510
But the filming ain't goin' well.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.940
It's definitely 'cause of a Bad Item.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:40.410
I think that the things Hadzuki-chan's father are using are the most suspicious.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.600
Those are the only things we haven't checked.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.490
Hey, I have a good idea.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:05.190
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:11.240
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.570
New director items, appear!

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.910
Maybe they're a bit too flowery.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.910
It should be fine.

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:26.880
His cute daughter is helpin' him, so he'll definitely agree to usin' 'em.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.090
I hope so.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:37.020
No... Something is still missing.

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:37.850
Papa?

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.560
Hadzuki, I'm still working, don't bother me.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.500
What are those for?

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:49.560
I have a new chair, sunglasses, and megaphone that I want you to use, Papa.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:54.680
You may not like them, but I want you to use them no matter what.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.240
Even if it's just for today.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:57.390
But...

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:01.910
Please, Papa, this is for you. Trust me.

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:10.700
This chair, this megaphone, and these sunglasses...

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.820
I've filmed with these for so many years.

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:16.800
These are Papa's important work partners.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:23.230
But, since Hadzuki says so, I'll listen to you, and use yours.

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.690
Papa.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:29.040
This is the first time I've seen Hadzuki push for something so hard.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:33.150
Papa doesn't know what's going on, but I'm sure there must be a reason for this.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.020
Yes.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.110
Thank you.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.950
It's a bit flowery for Papa.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.310
But I'm happy.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:44.670
You've poured your feelings for me into these things.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:47.240
Now the filming should go much better.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.360
Papa.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:49.600
Okay, it's getting late.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:52.380
You should get home. Mama's worried about you.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.070
Okay.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.140
Now, Oyaji, which one is the Bad Item?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.970
Ya better check 'em well!

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.980
The Bad Item...

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.040
Is...

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:07.770
Is?

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.110
None of them!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.520
No way!

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:15.780
Impossible!

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.650
No is no!

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.620
Then what could the Bad Item be?

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:24.290
Isn't it your mission to find it?

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.820
But is there anything left to check...?

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:32.040
Director! If you don't film this scene today, we'll be behind schedule.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:35.460
I guess we should film it like this then.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.920
Then can we start?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:39.380
Yeah.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.100
We're starting now!

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:50.010
Oh yeah, that thing that actress is wearing.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.860
I haven't checked that yet.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:54.570
Oh yeah, yer right.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.580
But they're starting already.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:01.580
Then let's transform and get near her.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:02.480
Transform into what?

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:06.070
What do you think when I say "Summer nights at the river?"

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.870
Pretty Witchy Aiko-chi!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.990
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.770
Pretty Witchy Doremi-chi!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:36.160
Pirika Pirilala Poporina Peperuto!

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:42.790
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:48.580
Pameruku Laruku Larilori Poppun!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.840
Turn into fireflies!

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.360
Now we can see in the dark.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:06.900
That's it!

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:09.850
Is it this?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.400
What about the earrings?

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.480
Still not it?

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.610
Let me see the sandals next.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.400
Yes, keep going, this take is perfect!

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.680
You're right director, this really is a very nice take.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:35.830
Ahhh, Koyuri-chan is so beautiful.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.630
What are you saying!?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.770
You just wanted to look at that actress! None of that stuff was a Bad Item at all!

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:44.300
But wasn't she nice...?

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.470
I got to be so close to Koyuri-chan. It was the best!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:48.900
Don't tell me...

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:51.680
You were lying when you said there were Bad Items here?

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:57.110
Oyaji!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.510
Hey!

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:00.100
Hadzuki, you're still here.

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:01.820
Papa.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.810
I got a very nice take.

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:07.660
It was all thanks to these director items you gave me.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:13.180
Well, it was actually because of those three fireflies.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:14.350
Fireflies?

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:17.290
Okay, I'll do my best tomorrow, too!

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:19.250
Just wait a little bit more.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.940
When I'm done, we'll go home together!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:25.980
Oh well.

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:26.760
Yeah.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:29.470
Thank goodness, thank goodness.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.970
Don't lie to us again like that!

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:48.560
In the end, we didn't find any Bad Items.

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:51.000
That's fine, the movie's a big hit.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:51.550
Yeah.

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:54.650
Okay, let's try even harder next time!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:06.070
On the tennis court, Kashiwagi-kun is hitting a golden tennis ball.

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:09.850
The scent of the blueberries and the twinkling stars in the sky is supporting my love.

00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:12.640
I love Kashiwagi-kun!

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:15.330
My heart beats into a panicked frenzy whenever I think of him.

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:18.810
Ahhh! To Kashiwagi-kun, I send you, my Love Smash!

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:20.530
Will she succeed this time!?

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:22.430
I hope she doesn't get heartbroken again.

00:22:22.430 --> 00:22:23.600
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:25.780
Love is a Windy Ride Over a Plateau.

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:28.730
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
